# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — handleDisconnect override slot.
#
# A client may replace the lobby's disconnect hook with its own:
# `Realm.handleDisconnect = function() { ... }` installs on the session's
# own globals and wins over the default on the Lobby prototype.  This
# fixture pins the install path — the slot takes, and the body runs.
#
# The on-destroy invocation is not pinned by an assertion here because it
# happens after the last expectation line: repl-chk-driver ends every
# fixture by finishing the client and sweeping once, which runs the hook
# on every session in the corpus.  A hook that crashed or leaked would
# show up under the sanitizers, corpus-wide.

# Install override, then call it directly to confirm it's wired up and
# the body runs (mutates Global.dx to 42).

## mode: repl
> {"id":19,"op":"eval","code":"Realm.handleDisconnect = function() { Global.dx = 42 } | Realm.handleDisconnect() | Global.dx"}
< "id":19 | "kind":"result" | "value":"42"
< "id":19 | "kind":"done"
